course: dictionary
lesson: 1115
title: Brazilian: a place, a person, a language
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Brazilian is a word about Brazil, the largest country in South America. It can describe things from Brazil, like «Brazilian football», or it can name a person from Brazil.
explain: Look at the words around it to find out which job it is doing. «Why do Brazilians speak Portuguese while their neighbours speak Spanish?» The word Brazilians has an s on the end, so it means several people from Brazil, and «their neighbours» tells you they live in a country next to others.
explain: Notice the capital B. Brazilian is linked to the name of a country, so it always starts with a capital letter. In «The Brazilian wandering spider is one of the most venomous spiders», the word tells you where the spider comes from.
fact: Brazil is the largest country in South America.
fact: As an adjective, «Brazilian» means from or to do with Brazil, as in «Brazilian football».
fact: A «Brazilian» is a person from Brazil, and the plural is «Brazilians».
fact: «Brazilian Portuguese» is the kind of Portuguese spoken in Brazil.
fact: Many people in Brazil speak Portuguese, not Spanish, and Brazil has the Amazon rainforest.
exercise: «Brazilian football» is famous all over the world. What does Brazilian mean here? | *From or to do with Brazil | A large country in Africa | A kind of dance | From or to do with Portugal
exercise: Lucas says, «Why do Brazilians speak Portuguese?» What is a Brazilian? | A type of football | *A person from Brazil | A sort of rainforest tree | A language spoken in Spain
exercise: Why does Brazilian start with a capital B? | *It is linked to the name of a country | It starts every new sentence | It is a long word | It is the name of a spider
test: «The Brazilian wandering spider is one of the most venomous spiders.» What does venomous mean? | Big and hairy | Very fast | Fond of bananas | *Able to give a poisonous bite or sting
test: The text says «bites are rare and an antivenom exists.» What does antivenom suggest? | A kind of banana | *A medicine that helps after a venomous bite | A night-time song | A web that catches flies
exam: Which sentence uses Brazilian to describe a thing, not a person? | «The Brazilian ran onto the field.» | «Two Brazilians spoke to the class.» | *«Brazilian carnival is loud and colourful.»
